# .trivyignore
#
# Each entry must include a justification so reviewers can verify the
# suppression is intentional and the reasoning remains valid over time.
# Re-evaluate all entries on each major dependency upgrade.

# CVE-2019-10768 — AngularJS prototype pollution in merge()
# Package : angular 0.0.0 (AngularJS 1.x, not Angular 2+)
# Source  : transitive dependency pulled in by metaapi.cloud-sdk
# Reason  : AngularJS is never loaded or executed in this Node.js process.
#           The vulnerable code path (client-side template rendering) has no
#           server-side attack surface. No fix is available without replacing
#           the MetaAPI SDK itself.
CVE-2019-10768

# CVE-2023-46233 / GHSA-xwcq-pm8m-c4vf — crypto-js: PBKDF2 1,000x weaker than specified
# Package : crypto-js 4.1.1 (fixed in 4.2.0)
# Source  : nested dependency bundled inside metaapi.cloud-sdk's own node_modules.
#           Not reachable by npm audit fix — only resolvable by downgrading
#           metaapi.cloud-sdk to v23 (breaking change).
# Reason  : crypto-js is used internally by the MetaAPI SDK for WebSocket
#           message signing — not for any PBKDF2 key derivation exposed to
#           this application. Re-evaluate when metaapi.cloud-sdk updates crypto-js.
CVE-2023-46233
GHSA-xwcq-pm8m-c4vf

# CVE-2021-23358 — underscore: arbitrary code execution via _.template()
# Package : underscore 1.4.4 (fixed in 1.12.1)
# Source  : transitive dependency of metaapi.cloud-sdk
# Reason  : The vulnerability requires an attacker to control the template
#           string passed to _.template(). The MetaAPI SDK uses underscore
#           as an internal utility library; no user-supplied data reaches
#           _.template() in this server-side process.
#           Scoped overrides failed to reach this package without breaking
#           the SDK. Re-evaluate when metaapi.cloud-sdk updates underscore.
CVE-2021-23358

# GHSA-r5fr-rjxr-66jc — lodash: Code injection via _.template imports key names
# GHSA-f23m-r3pf-42rh — lodash: Prototype pollution via array path bypass
# Package : lodash (transitive dep of metaapi.cloud-sdk)
# Reason  : Fixing requires downgrading metaapi.cloud-sdk to v23.1.1, which
#           removes the streaming connection API used by this application.
#           lodash is used internally by the MetaAPI SDK — no user-controlled
#           input is passed to _.template() or _.unset() in this process.
CVE-2021-23337
CVE-2022-31167

# GHSA-6fx8-h7jm-663j — parseuri: ReDoS via crafted URI string
# Package : parseuri (transitive dep via socket.io-client in metaapi.cloud-sdk)
# Reason  : Same constraint — only fixable via breaking metaapi.cloud-sdk
#           downgrade. The vulnerable URI parser is used internally by the
#           MetaAPI SDK's WebSocket layer; no user-supplied URIs reach it.
CVE-2022-3627

# GHSA-cf4h-3jhx-xvhq — underscore: Arbitrary code execution via _.template()
# GHSA-qpx9-hpmf-5gmw — underscore: Unlimited recursion DoS in _.flatten/_.isEqual
# Package : underscore (transitive dep of metaapi.cloud-sdk)
# Reason  : Same constraint as above. Already documented for CVE-2021-23358;
#           these are additional advisories for the same package/version.
#           Re-evaluate when metaapi.cloud-sdk updates its dependencies.
CVE-2021-23358
CVE-2024-45796